cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RECAST, please cite it as below."
title: "RECAST: reference-conditioned attribution of single-cell transcriptomes"
abstract: >-
  RECAST ranks the genes that distinguish a target cell population from a
  user-chosen reference population. It runs Integrated Gradients on a
  pretrained single-cell encoder along the path from the reference
  mean-expression profile to the target profile, and attributes the projected
  encoder-output change to individual genes. The same attributions score
  curated gene programs in new cells. The package provides adapters for
  SCimilarity, SSL (scTab, PBMC), scFoundation and scVI encoders, a
  command-line interface and a single-file script.
type: software
